    {
      "complexity": "complex",
      "detailed_figure_description": "A closed-loop circuit is drawn as a traffic-jam analogy. Small rectangular vehicles or particles marked “e⁻” crowd around the loop. A zigzag resistor labeled R is at the top, and a battery labeled V is at the bottom, with a plus sign on the left terminal and a minus sign on the right terminal.",
